WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:02.820
JOANNA SMITH: Hi.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.690
I'm Joanna Smith.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.232
And I'm going to show you how
to leverage the power of Google

00:00:06.232 --> 00:00:08.700
to enhance product discovery,
increase basket size,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.160
and create a seamless
omnichannel journey for grocery

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.900
shoppers.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.100
COVID-19 has disrupted
how we approach

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.890
many of our regular tasks.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.570
With grocery shopping,
a common errand

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.060
has been suddenly transformed
by safety concerns

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.140
and social distancing
requirements.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.170
So it's no wonder that
online grocery shopping

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.420
is expected to accelerate
at a much higher rate

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.722
than previous years.

00:00:28.722 --> 00:00:30.180
To set the scene
for this demo, I'm

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.090
going to take you through the
journey of a grocery shopper.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.520
Remy lives in the city with
a stay-at-home advisory

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.890
and has been finding
ways to avoid going out.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.020
This weekend he has plans
to do a virtual dinner

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.880
party with some friends,
where they will all

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.760
attempt to cook the same
meal over a video call.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.250
To find a fun recipe, Remy
has been browsing YouTube

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.170
for ideas and inspiration.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.820
He really likes
this homemade pizza

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.070
and checks the video description
for the recipe, where

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.290
he finds a link prompting
him to buy the ingredients

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.130
with Groceries For You.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:00.140
This video happens to be a
co-promotion with a retailer.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.550
And that link acts as
an entry point for Remy

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.820
to do his grocery shopping
online, making it easy for Remy

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.080
to shop for the
ingredients he will need.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.770
In the Groceries
For You app, Remy

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.540
is brought directly
to the recipe card

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.357
for the pizza he was looking at.

00:01:14.357 --> 00:01:16.440
Since he may already have
some of the ingredients,

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.140
he's offered an easy way to
select what he needs and then

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.540
add everything to his cart.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.370
In the cart, he's
given the opportunity

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.100
to make modifications and
add additional items based

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:30.010
on personalized recommendations
powered by machine learning.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.580
For example, he can select
a different mozzarella

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.650
from a brand he prefers.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.320
He can add related
items and even add

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.600
some of his go-to favorites.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.075
This experience was powered by
Google Cloud Recommendations

00:01:42.075 --> 00:01:43.350
AI.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.350
The retailer was able to offer
suggestions in several ways,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.120
first by looking
at similar items

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.340
and providing
comparable products,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.110
next by looking at
the customer's cart

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.000
and launching real-time
recommendations based

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.450
on selected items, and lastly,
by using historical user

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.770
data for predictive
replenishment suggestions.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.640
With Recommendations
AI, retailers

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.040
don't need to build their
own machine learning models.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.710
Instead they can plug their
product catalog and user

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.160
transaction data into existing
recommendations AI models

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.010
and be up and
running in no time.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.600
Early results from retailers
using Recommendations AI

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.100
show success, with more than
a 40% increase in conversion

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.530
driven by recommendations,
leading to more than a

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.850
50% increase in revenue
driven by recommendations.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.850
Remy is ready to
check out and selects

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.260
a window for curbside pickup
so that he can minimize

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.330
his exposure to other people.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.060
He uses G Pay, where his
payment information is already

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.855
securely stored
and avoids having

00:02:37.855 --> 00:02:39.480
to type out his credit
card information

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.830
on that mobile keyboard.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.510
When he's ready to
pickup his order,

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.520
Remy can easily
navigate to the store

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.470
and even share his
location with the retailer

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.840
to expedite the pickup process.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.180
Each of these pieces
offered a small improvement

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.460
that together created a seamless
journey for the customer.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:57.180
Later on, Remy is wondering
what to do if an item was

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.010
out of stock for his order.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.840
The app offers a
chat functionality.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.900
So Remy asks about the safety
precautions the store has,

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.390
in case he needs to go inside.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.550
The chat bot is able to
answer Remy's question

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:12.360
and explains the safety measures
the store has put in place.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.020
This helps Remy feel better.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.350
But he's hoping he
won't need to go inside.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:19.530
So he asks the chat bot what
the process is for substituting

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.970
items in his order.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.240
Again, the chat bot is is able
to answer Remy's question.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.760
And Remy is reassured that
his order will be complete,

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.030
since he has not received a
message indicating otherwise.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.310
This integrated digital
shopping assistant

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.070
is powered by Dialogflow,
the same technology that

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:37.410
supports Google Assistant.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.120
Dialogflow can be
used to easily train

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.220
a chat bot to answer
common questions

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.060
or even provide item details
based on your product catalog.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.850
At the store, the retailer
has mechanisms in place

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.380
to properly receive, execute,
and complete Remy's order.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.100
A grocery agent
receives the order

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.250
and collects all of the items,
with guidance on specific aisle

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.130
and shelf locations, handling
instructions, and even

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.770
the ability to scan on the go.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.410
Meanwhile, the store manager
can see data and metrics

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.620
for the entire store, including
information on gross sales

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.050
or the overall number of
orders received and completed

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.430
throughout the day.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.980
By combining data from
various sources like this,

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.990
the store manager can
make informed decisions

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.240
for things like
scheduling or inventory,

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.130
leading to more
satisfied customers,

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.920
lower wait times, and
fewer out-of-stock alerts.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.990
With this assisted
grocery experience,

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.000
Remy was able to go
from watching a YouTube

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.370
video of a recipe that
he liked to picking up

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.030
his groceries in a seamless
shopping experience.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.130
By bringing together
consumer Google products,

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.130
like YouTube maps and G Pay,
and leveraging Google Cloud

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.430
solutions like Recommendations
AI and Contact Center AI,

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:44.400
we hope to help your business
create positive and profitable

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.780
user experiences.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.390
To learn more about Google
Cloud's retail solutions,

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.411
check out cloud.google.com
/solutions/retail.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:57.080
[MUSIC FADING OUT]

